00:18:34,918 --> 00:18:40,342
But what is the point of increasing frequency if it becomes so much more difficult to get to a bus stop?

208
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:44,509
Is the T's motto more buses, less access?

209
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:49,430
Public transportation is for the public, is supposed to be accessible.

210
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:51,311
That should be the priority.

211
00:18:52,071 --> 00:18:58,412
There are numerous reasons why eliminating all bus stops along George Street and Winthrop Street is a terrible idea.

212
00:18:59,132 --> 00:19:05,413
This bus is usually crowded at any time of day in both directions, sometimes with standing room only.

213
00:19:05,973 --> 00:19:09,614
What are all these riders supposed to do if you get rid of all these stops?

214
00:19:10,314 --> 00:19:12,995
The 96 bus has a diverse ridership.

215
00:19:13,395 --> 00:19:19,839
They depend on this bus for work, for doctor appointments, for vet appointments, for school, for shopping, etc.

216
00:19:20,579 --> 00:19:25,901
Most do not have cars and they do not have someone to drive them to a more distant bus stop.

217
00:19:26,762 --> 00:19:31,424
On this route, there are lots of elderly people like myself and my husband.

218
00:19:31,814 --> 00:19:34,715
who are unable to walk very far or very well.

219
00:19:35,295 --> 00:19:38,896
To eliminate our bus stop would create unnecessary hardship.

220
00:19:39,616 --> 00:19:43,537
The 96 bus includes lots of seniors like myself and my husband.

221
00:19:44,018 --> 00:19:46,238
We have lived here over 25 years.

222
00:19:46,298 --> 00:19:50,339
We bought this house because it was close to the 96 bus stop.

223
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:54,801
We needed a bus that goes to Davis Square, Porter Square and Harvard Square.

224
00:19:55,301 --> 00:19:58,822
We would not have chosen this house if the bus stop was further away.

225
00:19:59,582 --> 00:20:02,543
Many of our neighbors chose their homes for the same reason.

226
00:20:02,983 --> 00:20:05,344
This includes old and new residents alike.

227
00:20:06,304 --> 00:20:10,065
Several riders who use this 96 bus are disabled.

228
00:20:10,686 --> 00:20:14,127
It is unfair and cruel to make them walk further to a bus stop.

229
00:20:15,007 --> 00:20:24,850
On the 96 bus, there are students who don't drive, people with shopping carts, riders with heavy or bulky bags, parents with baby strollers and young children,

230
00:20:25,314 --> 00:20:29,796
people who bring their pets to the vet and who go to various doctor appointments themselves.

231
00:20:30,376 --> 00:20:33,957
How are all these people supposed to cope with the T's proposed changes?

232
00:20:34,457 --> 00:20:38,619
They all need access to the bus stops along George Street and Winthrop Street.

233
00:20:39,639 --> 00:20:45,622
Imagine how difficult it would be walking much further in the pouring rain.

234
00:20:46,322 --> 00:20:48,783
And let's not forget about winter in New England.

235
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:52,372
Then there were the several snow storms during the winter.

236
00:20:52,773 --> 00:20:56,756
Most sidewalks remain only partially cleared throughout the winter.

237
00:20:57,377 --> 00:21:00,820
Impassable piles of ice and snow remain on street corners.

238
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:04,963
Walking a longer distance on ice is treacherous for everyone.

239
00:21:05,664 --> 00:21:13,050
Many people will be forced to walk in the street, which puts both the pedestrian and the driver at serious risk.

240
00:21:13,651 --> 00:21:15,873
This is an accident waiting to happen.

241
00:21:16,789 --> 00:21:21,832
Some years ago, a woman was raped walking from the bus stop near Boston Ave and Winthrop Street.

242
00:21:22,413 --> 00:21:26,815
Walking further, especially at night, poses a terrible and unnecessary risk.

243
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:33,860
The MBTA says that its goal is to have no one walk more than a quarter mile to a bus stop.

244
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:37,622
My husband and I would need to walk a mile with this new route.

245
00:21:38,363 --> 00:21:41,985
The proposed changes to the 96 bus route are indefensible.

246
00:21:42,425 --> 00:21:44,747
There is no justification for these changes.

247
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:51,760
Thank you.

248
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:53,843
Anyone else like to speak?

249
00:21:58,430 --> 00:21:59,252
Name and address for the record.

250
00:21:59,292 --> 00:22:01,275
Mary Anna Ducey, 2 Nod Street, Medford.

251
00:22:02,302 --> 00:22:06,586
I appeared before the city council on your June 14 meeting.

252
00:22:06,666 --> 00:22:13,653
That was when the first announcement was sent out over the phone that the public was, MBTA was gonna make proposed changes.

253
00:22:14,514 --> 00:22:18,618
Since then, I've talked to a lot of people in my neighborhood.

254
00:22:20,290 --> 00:22:23,352
Hardly anyone knew about these changes, which I brought up before.

255
00:22:24,192 --> 00:22:30,155
So one of my neighbors and I decided to do a petition that we've taken around our neighborhood.

256
00:22:31,796 --> 00:22:44,103
My neighbor plus two other residents that I've learned in the last month have also put up notices at all the bus stops, informing the riders and other residents that these proposed changes were happening.

257
00:22:45,203 --> 00:22:47,845
So just so you know, to date,

258
00:22:49,925 --> 00:22:59,092
I have 1,200 signatures on a petition opposing the three changes to the three buses, the 94, the 80, and the 96.

259
00:23:02,054 --> 00:23:14,203
Most people said that they moved here or bought their houses here, like this lady just said, because of the access of public transportation.

260
00:23:16,531 --> 00:23:19,553
A lot of people are very concerned about this.

261
00:23:19,813 --> 00:23:22,735
They've structured their whole lives around public transit.

262
00:23:22,915 --> 00:23:28,518
Talked to a lady yesterday who does her banking in Cambridge and she uses the 96 bus to get there.

263
00:23:28,558 --> 00:23:30,179
She's lived in Medford for 50 years.

264
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:35,302
So everybody has structured their lives around this public transportation.

265
00:23:36,043 --> 00:23:39,045
A lot of parents send their kids to Arlington Catholic.

266
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:46,302
and they take the 80 bus to Owings and Center, which is not gonna be there if they terminate that service.

267
00:23:47,323 --> 00:23:50,604
So it's gonna be a big hardship if these changes happen.

268
00:23:53,865 --> 00:24:05,089
People have also sent in their own comments to the T in addition to this petition, but they thanked me, not that I'm looking for thanks, but they thanked me for doing this because otherwise their voices would not be heard.

269
00:24:06,076 --> 00:24:15,721
Now, as a coincidence, I bumped into Pat Jelen about a week and a half ago at Walgreens in Somerville, and I asked her, Pat, I said what's happening with these buses.

270
00:24:16,282 --> 00:24:20,384
She rolled her eyes and she said, I know poor communication I said yes.

271
00:24:21,125 --> 00:24:25,067
She's also finding that in Somerville, because they're eliminating some buses in Somerville.

272
00:24:26,170 --> 00:24:39,096
So, I said well Pat I've been going around the neighborhood with the petition and I told her but you know nobody knew about it and so forth so she stopped and she said you have a petition I said yes, she says how many signatures do you have what that time I had 800, she says 800.

273
00:24:39,136 --> 00:24:39,577
I said yes 800.

274
00:24:42,498 --> 00:24:48,904
She says, Would you like to come into the State House and present this will get the Department of Transportation to come and so forth.

275
00:24:49,405 --> 00:24:50,025
I said sure.

276
00:24:50,846 --> 00:25:00,996
So, anyway, my neighbor has been in back and forth with her emailing her, her chief of staff, and they're very busy right now because this is the end of their legislative session.

277
00:25:01,857 --> 00:25:09,220
So we're not sure if we're going to be able to get into the State House before the end of the legislative session or afterwards.

278
00:25:09,260 --> 00:25:17,504
But my neighbor and I will deposit these petitions with the MBTA before the 31st of this month.

279
00:25:18,024 --> 00:25:23,827
If we have this meeting with Pat Jelen and whoever else, she was going to call the media or whoever else to bring attention to this.

280
00:25:24,818 --> 00:25:28,181
So she was pretty upset about this too.

281
00:25:28,622 --> 00:25:35,288
So I just wanted to update you on what's transpired with me since I was here a month ago.

282
00:25:37,630 --> 00:25:42,295
And some of the comments that people say was, this is supposed to be public transit.

283
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:43,095
It's for the public.

284
00:25:45,097 --> 00:25:50,118
Even if the state has to fund this at a loss, they should provide this service.

285
00:25:50,138 --> 00:25:51,478
They should not be cutting service.

286
00:25:51,978 --> 00:25:53,879
Not everybody wants to go into Boston.

287
00:25:53,939 --> 00:25:56,199
People use these buses to commute around the city.

288
00:25:57,839 --> 00:26:01,040
So it's important that they maintain these buses where they are.

289
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:07,321
So that's it in a nutshell, but I just wanted to update you all on what's happened in the last month.

290
00:26:08,161 --> 00:26:08,461
Thank you.

291
00:26:08,481 --> 00:26:09,342
And thank you for your hard work.

292
00:26:09,542 --> 00:26:10,202
Vice President Paris.

293
00:26:10,562 --> 00:26:11,042
Madam President.

294
00:26:14,123 --> 00:26:18,106
I just want to again echo that thank you for collecting all of the signatures.

295
00:26:18,727 --> 00:26:23,310
Would it be possible potentially, if I am going to give the city council a copy.

296
00:26:23,570 --> 00:26:28,294
Great, because I was just gonna say we may be have a copier downstairs we can use already made.

297
00:26:29,035 --> 00:26:31,637
In addition to the original three other copies so.

298
00:26:32,477 --> 00:26:37,900
So I anticipated that I was going to give one to the city council just so you know, fantastic.

299
00:26:37,940 --> 00:26:45,544
But I mean most of these I haven't, I've done a little bit in West Medford, most of these are hillside residents because that's where the biggest impact of this is.

300
00:26:46,476 --> 00:26:50,117
If I have time before the deadline, I will go to West Medford also.

301
00:26:50,738 --> 00:26:55,199
But with the weather, I usually only go out a couple of hours after supper every night.

302
00:26:55,339 --> 00:26:59,541
So this is the result of a couple of hours after supper every night.

303
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:02,402
That's how willing people are to sign this thing.

304
00:27:03,403 --> 00:27:05,543
So that's a statement in and of itself.

305
00:27:06,104 --> 00:27:07,204
Great, thank you so much.

306
00:27:07,364 --> 00:27:07,724
Thank you.

