00:27:30,384 --> 00:27:32,085
Hello, let's see.

314
00:27:32,225 --> 00:27:35,268
I don't know if I can put my video on.

315
00:27:35,348 --> 00:27:38,451
Sorry, probably I don't know how.

316
00:27:39,712 --> 00:27:42,714
Well, I'm just gonna second what was already said because,

317
00:27:44,518 --> 00:27:46,219
I live in the Hillside neighborhood.

318
00:27:46,439 --> 00:27:47,339
I depend upon the 96.

319
00:27:47,959 --> 00:27:52,920
I moved here precisely for the transportation.

320
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:58,362
I really don't have much to add because the last two public speakers were so eloquent.

321
00:27:59,042 --> 00:28:03,804
I'm also a senior citizen and I don't have good knees.

322
00:28:03,964 --> 00:28:05,864
I can't walk to Davis Square.

323
00:28:05,944 --> 00:28:09,785
Now, what am I gonna have to go up to that tough stop?

324
00:28:09,865 --> 00:28:10,866
That's the green line.

325
00:28:10,906 --> 00:28:12,126
That does me no good at all.

326
00:28:13,649 --> 00:28:15,133
How do I get the Harvard Square.

327
00:28:15,153 --> 00:28:18,062
Um, those are the places I go.

328
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:22,761
that's where I have to take the bus to work.

329
00:28:22,881 --> 00:28:31,667
So now I don't know how to get to work, but you know, okay, so I'm close to retirement, but what about my neighborhood?

330
00:28:32,187 --> 00:28:46,296
I have seen in the past 10 years, the entire street I live on is now filled with young people, young couples who are taking the bus and they precisely bought their houses in this neighborhood.

331
00:28:47,433 --> 00:28:48,354
Because of the bus.

332
00:28:49,054 --> 00:28:58,320
So I just think it's, I don't understand the logic behind this, but I have to say I've also been through so many of these things and no matter how much we complain.

333
00:28:58,340 --> 00:29:02,502
The MBTA is going to do absolutely nothing.

334
00:29:02,942 --> 00:29:04,864
So my question is what is.

335
00:29:05,908 --> 00:29:11,910
the city council, what are the tools that the city council has to fight this?

336
00:29:12,270 --> 00:29:27,275
Does it have to go through representative jail into the state house or can the city council stand up and say, we won't put up with this and then ask the community to get behind the city council?

337
00:29:27,916 --> 00:29:29,156
So that's what I would say.

338
00:29:29,676 --> 00:29:31,657
Thank you very much for your attention.

339
00:29:32,817 --> 00:29:33,317
Thank you, Barbara.

340
00:29:33,337 --> 00:29:36,278
And then if I could just get your name and address for the record for us.

341
00:29:36,478 --> 00:29:39,899
Barbara Corbett, 68 Brookings Street.

342
00:29:40,939 --> 00:29:41,379
Thank you.

343
00:29:42,020 --> 00:29:43,420
Madam President.

344
00:29:44,380 --> 00:29:46,561
Thank you, Barbara, for your input.

345
00:29:48,601 --> 00:29:50,362
Sometimes you wish we had more power.

346
00:29:51,222 --> 00:29:57,044
Unfortunately, we're at the same frustrations that you are.

347
00:29:58,884 --> 00:30:00,125
Our voice can only

348
00:30:03,208 --> 00:30:07,711
express your concerns to our state delegates, and hopefully they can get things done.

349
00:30:07,751 --> 00:30:10,873
But unfortunately, even there, you see the difficulties.

350
00:30:11,113 --> 00:30:13,495
I mean, so it's been very frustrating.

351
00:30:14,856 --> 00:30:25,983
Believe me, as the chairperson for the Subcommittee on Transportation, there are times when I've wanted to not send payment, not held back on what we can do.

352
00:30:26,044 --> 00:30:29,086
But unfortunately, the law states we can't do that.

353
00:30:30,614 --> 00:30:41,552
We can't do some of these, these, these actions so it's difficult, it's very frustrating, but it's.

354
00:30:42,829 --> 00:30:51,194
And I can only imagine when you live on one of those routes and it's play such a negative impact on your quality of life.

355
00:30:51,754 --> 00:31:05,502
You know, from what I'm hearing, a lot of people that I've talked to are senior citizens who have had these routes for virtually a whole time in Medford.

356
00:31:06,142 --> 00:31:12,266
And now the T is going to just uproot everyone without truly their input.

357
00:31:13,052 --> 00:31:22,037
And like Councilor Caviello says, this is something that was already been done years in advance when they started talking about the Green Line extension.

358
00:31:22,557 --> 00:31:27,600
So that's even disheartening because this, again, here we are talking about this when?

359
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:29,361
In July.

360
00:31:30,182 --> 00:31:31,002
Who's really listening?

361
00:31:32,403 --> 00:31:33,183
Who's really listening?

362
00:31:34,404 --> 00:31:36,265
Look at the respect we get from the T tonight.

363
00:31:36,945 --> 00:31:38,306
You can't even jump on a 45 minute Zoom

364
00:31:40,665 --> 00:31:48,573
You know, maybe you could be at your cottage in the Cape, you could still jump on a Zoom and understand the ramifications of these changes.

365
00:31:49,574 --> 00:32:03,507
And like we've said, this city is one of the top paying communities in the Commonwealth to the T. You know, in the past, I've asked the city solicitor to see if we can freeze all funding toward the T

366
00:32:04,800 --> 00:32:09,121
because we're not getting any feedback back because we don't have that power.

367
00:32:09,221 --> 00:32:19,423
So I share your frustration and it's, you know, all we can do is keep pounding the surveys, keep reaching out to your state delegates.

368
00:32:19,983 --> 00:32:32,966
And again, when you hear the comment that even after the next round comes out, there won't be any public discussions, they're having only one forum and that's passed.

369
00:32:33,997 --> 00:32:35,898
is just disgusting, it's disheartening.

370
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:57,547
So I share in your frustration and I'll keep pushing with every ounce of being that we have to contact the governor's office and push with the state delegates and know that, listen, in my eyes, it affects one member of this community

371
00:32:59,795 --> 00:33:00,816
It's all off or not.

372
00:33:00,936 --> 00:33:07,019
I think that the comment that was made, this all that we made was that this is public transportation.

373
00:33:07,860 --> 00:33:12,662
I think they forgot that the most important word there is public, not transportation.

374
00:33:13,143 --> 00:33:14,043
It's for the public.

375
00:33:15,584 --> 00:33:18,025
And we're missing a huge piece here by making these moves.

376
00:33:18,165 --> 00:33:25,290
So, you know, it's great that they have all these forums and they have these surveys, but I share in your frustration.

377
00:33:25,350 --> 00:33:29,352
I'm a city councilor and I'm saying, geez, the T's gonna do what they wanna do anyway.

378
00:33:30,407 --> 00:33:32,148
So again, Bob or Ms.

379
00:33:32,188 --> 00:33:44,954
Corbett, I share in your frustration and that's why I was hoping there'd be a member of the team that we can look and talk to and say, these are real people that you're affecting.

380
00:33:45,514 --> 00:33:51,817
Because all they see is in a boardroom, they sit in a room and they say, ah, let's cut this one, let's cut that one, that fits, great.

381
00:33:52,418 --> 00:33:53,038
And they move on.

382
00:33:54,484 --> 00:33:56,185
They don't see the people sitting in the audience.

383
00:33:56,205 --> 00:33:57,285
They don't see the people at Zoom.

384
00:33:57,785 --> 00:34:14,270
And they don't realize that, you know, when there's three inches of snow and you're a senior citizen and you have bad knees, and now you have to detour your process of living to something that just really cripples you is disheartening.

385
00:34:14,630 --> 00:34:16,751
So thank you, Madam President.

386
00:34:16,771 --> 00:34:22,173
I'm sorry for going on, but this is a frustrating situation when it comes to this department and this Commonwealth.

387
00:34:24,281 --> 00:34:27,763
I do see Director Blake has his hand up to you.

388
00:34:28,183 --> 00:34:36,527
Just going to director of traffic and transportation, Todd Blake.

389
00:34:36,547 --> 00:34:37,048
I thank you.

390
00:34:37,688 --> 00:34:46,633
And I want to thank the council and everyone attending because the city really does need your feedback as well and I just wanted to highlight some things, general things to

391
00:34:48,187 --> 00:34:51,668
to be more fruitful with our feedback, which is exactly what I'm hearing tonight.

392
00:34:52,628 --> 00:34:58,810
I want to stress that there are many trade-offs and possibly many pros and cons.

393
00:34:58,870 --> 00:35:12,854
So I would encourage all to comment as much and as detailed as possible regarding both good and bad that may involve new connections or lost connections or frequency or diversions or

394
00:35:13,694 --> 00:35:21,138
the topographic issue that a lot of folks pointed out in Somerville and Medford where some of our communities have a lot of hills in them.

395
00:35:21,778 --> 00:35:28,041
And it seems like the approach was looking at it from a horizontal standpoint and not considering those challenges.

396
00:35:28,721 --> 00:35:35,385
So other things to point out that may not be obvious to folks is the span of service.

397
00:35:35,405 --> 00:35:39,667
So the span of service is when the first bus in the morning starts and the last bus in the evening ends.

398
00:35:40,467 --> 00:35:43,829
Some of the changes involve ending the last bus of the evening.

399
00:35:44,470 --> 00:35:50,353
So some that may have ended before at 12 31am may be ending at 7pm now.

400
00:35:50,754 --> 00:35:54,676
So just be on the lookout for that when you're looking at how it may impact you.

401
00:35:55,957 --> 00:35:56,658
Yeah, yeah.

402
00:35:57,798 --> 00:36:09,746
So some some blocks in some communities also may have been served by multiple routes before and may only be served by one, or if they are multiple, if the frequencies are less, it still may have

403
00:36:10,300 --> 00:36:12,621
a negative impact on you or an improvement on you.

404
00:36:12,661 --> 00:36:30,990
So yeah, I just encourage all to communicate with both the city and the MBTA with as detailed comments as possible so that if and when some future version comes out, maybe if there is some good in there, it can include the good and maybe eliminate the bad, hopefully.

405
00:36:32,010 --> 00:36:32,330
Thank you.

406
00:36:33,091 --> 00:36:33,791
Thank you, Director Blake.

407
00:36:34,071 --> 00:36:34,671
Vice President Behrs.

408
00:36:34,871 --> 00:36:35,692
Thank you, Madam President.

409
00:36:38,104 --> 00:36:50,848
I haven't completed my research on this, so take it with a grain of salt, but one thing that I am looking into is if a bus stop is moved, is there a city approval process for that?

410
00:36:50,868 --> 00:36:52,949
Does it go through the traffic commission?

411
00:36:52,989 --> 00:36:54,170
Does it go through the council?

412
00:36:54,730 --> 00:37:02,372
So that may be one, and maybe quite frankly, the only piece of leverage that the city may have within its processes around changing a bus route.

413
00:37:04,093 --> 00:37:16,800
I have had the idea, but haven't had the time to do the deep dive to see what that process is, but I am hoping to do that relatively soon as that could give us some ability to try to impact the changes.

414
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:21,663
Is that it?

415
00:37:22,403 --> 00:37:22,563
Yeah.

416
00:37:22,723 --> 00:37:24,124
Thank you, Representative Ferguson.

417
00:37:24,184 --> 00:37:26,765
Going to Jennifer Sullivan on Zoom.

418
00:37:27,486 --> 00:37:29,767
Name and address for the record, please, and I will unmute you.

419
00:37:31,088 --> 00:37:31,748
Hi, can you hear me?

420
00:37:32,647 --> 00:37:34,113
Yes, great.

421
00:37:34,234 --> 00:37:36,905
Jennifer Sullivan Marston street in Medford.

422
00:37:38,858 --> 00:37:42,060
So I won't belabor too much, because a lot of people have done a great job covering things.

423
00:37:42,620 --> 00:37:44,701
And I'm going to submit feedback and everything.

424
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:49,284
I agree that I'm really frustrated that nobody from the MBTA is here today.

425
00:37:51,885 --> 00:37:58,769
So I commute to Boston University, where I work, from the Marston Street stop.

426
00:37:58,929 --> 00:38:00,750
And I take the 96 to Harvard Square.

427
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:02,471
And then I take a bus from there to work.

428
00:38:02,891 --> 00:38:04,532
And then I do it on the way home as well.

429
00:38:04,652 --> 00:38:05,533
That's my commute.

430
00:38:06,433 --> 00:38:11,756
If this stops, it's going to really impact my quality of life and my job.

431
00:38:13,257 --> 00:38:14,898
So I have a lot of experience with this commute.

432
00:38:15,018 --> 00:38:19,520
And what's really frustrating for me with the MBTA is that I actually did one of those.

433
00:38:19,580 --> 00:38:28,025
I was one of their survey people where I got a survey, I think every week, asking me how my commute was, what could change, what could be better.

434
00:38:28,105 --> 00:38:29,766
And I did it for well over a year.

435
00:38:30,726 --> 00:38:39,770
So, and I eventually stopped because I just because I started hearing rumblings of things changing and I said you're not even listening Why am I even doing this every every like I have better things to do.

436
00:38:40,971 --> 00:38:48,455
But so what frustrates me is that, again, it's been said here that even when they asked for feedback they're not even looking at it.

437
00:38:50,330 --> 00:38:58,272
And I think a lot of these change, I attended one of the presentations that thankfully a lot of local residents attended as well.

438
00:38:59,092 --> 00:39:06,114
And a lot of these changes are relying on the red line running well, which is not accurate.

439
00:39:06,894 --> 00:39:11,655
I make a point to avoid the red line just because it's so temperamental and the stations are

440
00:39:12,265 --> 00:39:13,085
not in great shape.

441
00:39:14,786 --> 00:39:21,729
Several years ago, I tripped on a crack on the red line and shattered my ankle, and the MBTA never responded.

442
00:39:21,849 --> 00:39:26,472
So I just try to avoid things like that, and I'm a healthy person.

443
00:39:28,052 --> 00:39:37,957
So again, a couple of questions I just wanted to ask was, and these are sort of open-ended, is doesn't this impact

444
00:39:38,855 --> 00:39:42,056
the selling points of our houses.

445
00:39:42,656 --> 00:39:50,217
My parents bought this house because there was a bus that could take you to Davis, Porter, Harvard, things like that.

446
00:39:50,297 --> 00:39:54,958
I mean, having transit right there is a huge selling point.

447
00:39:56,898 --> 00:40:02,999
Also, I don't know if there's any local businesses or medical offices that can help us advocate for how needed these are.

448
00:40:03,019 --> 00:40:08,220
And then just my last point is in terms of accessibility,

449
00:40:09,580 --> 00:40:14,343
especially for older people, if the pandemic taught us anything, it's the dangers of isolation.

450
00:40:15,364 --> 00:40:29,112
And if it's such a pain to get somewhere, whether it's weather or just mental strength, because you're tired, people are going to put off going to appointments, going to see people.

451
00:40:30,653 --> 00:40:33,014
We need to be taking care of each other and keeping connected.

452
00:40:33,114 --> 00:40:37,837
And eliminating a lot of these stops is going to really impact that.

453
00:40:39,435 --> 00:40:39,836
Thanks again.

454
00:40:39,856 --> 00:40:41,998
Thank you, Miss Sullivan.

455
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:45,681
Is there anyone else who would like to speak tonight?

456
00:40:46,382 --> 00:40:47,023
Members of the public?

457
00:40:54,111 --> 00:40:57,774
I'm Wendy Mifflin again, still 18 Douglas Road, Medford.

458
00:40:58,875 --> 00:41:02,598
I have a question about the mayor's involvement.

459
00:41:02,858 --> 00:41:09,063
We get calls on a regular basis about snow removal and heat waves and street cleaning and events.

460
00:41:09,904 --> 00:41:16,489
And there's been no information about this meeting or anything having to do with the bus situation.

461
00:41:17,149 --> 00:41:22,554
I'm wondering why that is and if there's anything that can be done about that, because I don't think anybody knew about this.

462
00:41:23,542 --> 00:41:25,043
Thank you.

463
00:41:25,323 --> 00:41:30,767
And the other thing is, I'm wondering if there's other ways that we can get something happening.

464
00:41:31,368 --> 00:41:34,290
A friend of mine suggested writing a letter to the Globe.

465
00:41:34,390 --> 00:41:36,792
They print letters about various topics.

466
00:41:37,492 --> 00:41:45,919
And what about somehow talking to the news media, the various, you know, Channel 4, Channel whatever, the various Channel 5, whatever.

467
00:41:46,419 --> 00:41:49,621
I just feel like there's some way, I feel like this is so wrong.

468
00:41:50,422 --> 00:41:58,814
that there is that you know we have to throw everything against the wall and see what sticks and that there's got to be a good solution to this.

469
00:41:59,855 --> 00:42:00,536
Thank you.

470
00:42:00,836 --> 00:42:06,825
Director Blake, can you speak to the outreach that's been done on the from City Hall as far as alerting folks to this?

471
00:42:11,307 --> 00:42:11,867
Yes, thank you.

472
00:42:12,008 --> 00:42:23,996
I believe the city's communications department has posted on the city website, city social media accounts, and also I believe a reverse call went out to those who are signed up for that system.

473
00:42:25,677 --> 00:42:27,518
Do we know if there's any additional communication plan?

474
00:42:27,539 --> 00:42:33,403
I mean, I'm sure the council would be happy to make a motion to ask for that, but do we know if there's any additional communication plan with the deadline looming?

475
00:42:34,143 --> 00:42:38,887
Yeah, we can look into that and get back to you on any additional information.

476
00:42:38,967 --> 00:42:39,267
Correct.

477
00:42:39,347 --> 00:42:39,467
Yeah.

478
00:42:40,835 --> 00:42:41,335
Thank you, Ms.

479
00:42:41,355 --> 00:42:41,656
Ducey.

480
00:42:42,116 --> 00:42:46,880
Yeah, I'd like to say that not everybody has access to the website.

481
00:42:48,681 --> 00:42:53,045
And a lot of the people I talked to did not get a voicemail at all.

482
00:42:53,726 --> 00:42:55,847
So they probably don't have landlines.

483
00:42:55,927 --> 00:43:01,612
They probably have cell phones and they probably never registered their cell phones with the city to be contacted.

484
00:43:02,132 --> 00:43:08,558
So maybe the city should try to enlist people to get on board here so that they can get messages.

485
00:43:09,198 --> 00:43:14,140
Because right now, you know, it's not the city's fault if nobody's registered to get the message.

486
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:17,481
So you have to kind of recruit people to get on board here.

487
00:43:19,162 --> 00:43:21,323
So it's just a suggestion.

488
00:43:21,343 --> 00:43:23,864
Thank you for that.

489
00:43:26,735 --> 00:43:38,605
I just want to note as well that this council has requested that communications go out in multiple formats, that it not just be kind of digital only and hoping that everyone has access to them.

490
00:43:38,885 --> 00:43:40,526
That's a motion that we passed recently.

491
00:43:41,447 --> 00:43:54,617
And this is not anything to speak directly to Director Blake and the work that he's doing in his office, but, you know, with our Eversource meeting and with a few other meetings, we have had

492
00:43:55,892 --> 00:44:02,154
You know, all we can do is ask that something go out on the, as a council, all we can do is ask that something go out on the reverse 911.

493
00:44:02,234 --> 00:44:07,256
It's happened a couple of times, but most of the time it doesn't.

494
00:44:08,877 --> 00:44:16,480
I don't know what we can do to try to accelerate that or do better about that, but it has been an ongoing issue that we have been trying to get information out there.

495
00:44:16,540 --> 00:44:22,642
But at the end of the day, we don't control the communication channels of the city that mayor and the city administration do.

496
00:44:26,034 --> 00:44:28,315
Thank you for the first Councilor Carvel.

497
00:44:28,335 --> 00:44:29,495
You make a good point here.

498
00:44:30,355 --> 00:44:42,418
Unfortunately, you know, we no longer have a newspaper here anymore, which is which was, you know, maybe not a lot of people read it, but people read it online and they bought the paper, that newspaper is gone.

499
00:44:43,518 --> 00:44:47,179
The only paper we have, which is isn't really a paper is the patch.

500
00:44:47,919 --> 00:44:51,960
And how many people subscribe to the patch to get that and it's like you said, not everybody.

501
00:44:54,100 --> 00:44:55,741
has access to those things.

502
00:44:56,081 --> 00:45:06,727
But I think, and one of the other things, Joe, you said no one gets a call, but I think sometimes we get to the point where we get too many phone calls from the city and people ignore them.

503
00:45:07,127 --> 00:45:08,588
So I'll go out another call from the city again.

504
00:45:09,448 --> 00:45:12,591
You know, so that, you know, it's a little, it goes a little bit both ways.

505
00:45:12,611 --> 00:45:18,635
You know, sometimes we don't call them up and then other times we call too much and people just turn us off and they don't answer the phone.

506
00:45:19,256 --> 00:45:21,457
So that's, I think that's part of the problem too.

507
00:45:21,798 --> 00:45:27,362
But again, not having a newspaper here is really a big hurt to the city because nothing gets out anymore.

508
00:45:31,093 --> 00:45:40,548
Someone suggested to me that the city sends out four tax bills, real estate tax bills, and six water bills a year.

509
00:45:41,857 --> 00:45:48,321
If the city has enough advanced notice, they could put a notice in with the tax bill or the water bill.

510
00:45:48,441 --> 00:45:51,843
At least the homeowners would have some advanced notice.

511
00:45:51,863 --> 00:45:55,405
But as you say, it only goes to the homeowners, it doesn't, the renters.

512
00:45:55,425 --> 00:45:57,066
It would be more than what's happening now.

513
00:45:57,106 --> 00:46:03,430
Yes, but the renters, and we have a good amount of renters, they'll never get the notice either.

514
00:46:03,510 --> 00:46:06,752
I understand, but we're trying to get more than what we have now.

515
00:46:06,852 --> 00:46:08,253
So every little bit helps.

516
00:46:08,533 --> 00:46:11,255
I know we try, but again, it's either too much or not enough.

517
00:46:11,914 --> 00:46:12,955
Right, right.

518
00:46:13,055 --> 00:46:13,455
Thank you.

519
00:46:14,116 --> 00:46:14,416
Thank you.

520
00:46:14,596 --> 00:46:19,440
And I'm sure I'm preaching to the choir, but folks who may be watching who aren't signed up for city alerts, you can sign up for those.

521
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:27,426
If you go to the website medfordma.org and scroll down to alerts, you can sign up to get those on your cell phone if you're not already getting them on a landline or otherwise.

