525
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:48,023
So again, if you don't wanna speak tonight, but you do wanna make sure your comments get in, you can email mbtabus at medford-ma.gov.

526
00:46:48,703 --> 00:46:52,186
That would be the city collecting feedback to then respond to the MBTA.

527
00:46:52,566 --> 00:46:57,649
We're gonna be collecting all the comments that were made tonight, the city clerk, and we'll put that together to deliver it to the MBTA.

528
00:46:58,050 --> 00:47:03,654
And you can also go to the MBTA website and take the survey as well and reach out to, you know, Rep.

529
00:47:03,694 --> 00:47:03,974
Barber,

530
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:08,985
rep Garber Lee, rep Donato and let them know as well as Senator Jalen and let them know your feelings.

531
00:47:09,025 --> 00:47:11,087
So I know this puts a lot on the public.

532
00:47:11,708 --> 00:47:19,777
Ideally, you know, it would happen the other way where the MBTA is really working hard to solicit this but if folks can reach out any way they can, the more voices we get, hopefully, they will listen.

533
00:47:21,359 --> 00:47:23,141
And sorry, just checking.

534
00:47:23,161 --> 00:47:23,982
Okay.

535
00:47:26,215 --> 00:47:31,860
Um, just started this director, Blake just noting that other city departments have also posted elsewhere.

536
00:47:31,880 --> 00:47:40,327
For instance, this was there were notices posted in the housing facilities as far as these meetings and construction projects have flyers to shoot at them.

537
00:47:41,909 --> 00:47:43,450
Sometimes people mistake them from junk mail.

538
00:47:43,470 --> 00:47:48,173
So just Director Blake just sending me a chat mentioning some other ways that outreach has been performed.

539
00:47:49,194 --> 00:47:54,957
